From b3d3d7aa6df45e5630871e35ed2e9c3f7755b7e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:57:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: twl6030-irq: let the chained interrupts request wakeup
 again

twl6030_irq_set_wake() counts the wakeup-enabled TWL6030 interrupts, and
the PM notifier makes the TWL6030 interrupt line a wakeup source when
that count is non-zero. But the irq_chip is a copy of dummy_irq_chip,
which has had IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE since commit 10a50f1ab5f0
("genirq: Set IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE flag for dummy_irq_chip"), so the core
never calls twl6030_irq_set_wake(): the count stays 0, the parent
interrupt is never enabled for wakeup, and nothing behind the PMIC can
wake the system. On a Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1 (OMAP4430 + TWL6032) an
RTC alarm armed with /sys/class/rtc/rtc0/wakealarm fires (it is counted
after resume) but the tablet sleeps on until the power key is pressed.

Clear the flag on the copy.

Fixes: 10a50f1ab5f0 ("genirq: Set IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE flag for dummy_irq_chip")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c b/drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c
index 0ca00f618d4d..efa28416c2c3 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/twl6030-irq.c
@@ -331,6 +331,8 @@ int twl6030_init_irq(struct device *dev, int irq_num)
 	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.name = "twl6030";
 	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.irq_set_type = NULL;
 	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.irq_set_wake = twl6030_irq_set_wake;
+	/* dummy_irq_chip skips irq_set_wake, but the PIH needs to know */
+	twl6030_irq->irq_chip.flags &= ~IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE;
 
 	twl6030_irq->pm_nb.notifier_call = twl6030_irq_pm_notifier;
 	atomic_set(&twl6030_irq->wakeirqs, 0);
-- 
2.55.0

